+# Epic 6: CLI Management & Operations
+
+## Overview
+
+Epic 6 delivers the operator-facing command-line interface for Axiathon. It covers the CLI framework (clap 4.x), system status and health commands, configuration management, ingestion control, alert management, shell completions, server/daemon management, Prometheus metrics export, Grafana dashboards, zero-downtime upgrades, and capacity planning tools. Stories 6.1-6.7 are Core (MVP), stories 6.8-6.11 are Extended (Growth).
+
+**Priority:** P1
+**Repo:** axiathon
+**Stories:** 11 (48 points)
+**Jira Epic:** Not yet assigned
+
+## Planning Documents
+
+| Document | Relevant Sections |
+|----------|-------------------|
+| **BMAD Epic Doc** (`axiathon/_bmad-output/planning-artifacts/epics/epic-06-cli-management.md`) | All 11 stories with acceptance criteria, FR96-FR112, NFR84-NFR95, NFR320-NFR328 |
+| **CLI & TUI Architecture** (`axiathon/_bmad-output/planning-artifacts/architecture/core-architectural-decisions/cli-tui-architecture.md`) | Two-binary architecture, command groups, exit codes, SiemClient, credential storage, config file format |
+| **Configuration Management Architecture** (`axiathon/_bmad-output/planning-artifacts/architecture/core-architectural-decisions/configuration-management-architecture.md`) | config-rs v0.15, hierarchy, hot reload, secret management, validation, CLI integration |
+| **Observability & Capacity Planning Architecture** (`axiathon/_bmad-output/planning-artifacts/architecture/core-architectural-decisions/observability-capacity-planning-architecture.md`) | Metrics design, health checks, capacity forecasting, alerting architecture |
+| **Project Structure & Boundaries** (`axiathon/_bmad-output/planning-artifacts/architecture/project-structure-boundaries.md`) | Crate layout, binary split, dependency rules |
+| **Implementation Patterns & Consistency Rules** (`axiathon/_bmad-output/planning-artifacts/architecture/implementation-patterns-consistency-rules.md`) | Error handling, output formatting, testing patterns |
+
+## Background
+
+Axiathon requires an operator-facing CLI for day-to-day administration: checking system health, managing configuration, controlling ingestion pipelines, triaging alerts, and managing the server daemon lifecycle. The CLI must be scriptable (JSON/CSV output, exit codes) and operator-friendly (tab completion, colored tables, contextual help).
+
+The project uses a **two-binary architecture** following the docker/dockerd and kubectl/kube-apiserver pattern:
+
+- **`axiathon-server`** (crate: `axiathon-server`, formerly `axiathon-api`) runs on the server/container. Handles daemon lifecycle, migrations, config reload, and serves the HTTP API.
+- **`axiathon`** (crate: `axiathon-client`) runs on operator workstations. All commands talk to the server via HTTP API through the `SiemClient` wrapper.
+
+This separation means the client binary depends only on `axiathon-core` for shared types. It never imports server-side crates (storage, detection, ingestion, query). All data flows through HTTP.
+
+The Extended stories (6.8-6.11) add operational maturity: Prometheus-format metrics export, pre-built Grafana dashboards, rolling upgrade capability, and capacity forecasting. These target platform engineers managing production deployments.
+
+## Technical Architecture
+
+### Crate Layout
+
+```
+crates/axiathon-client/
+  Cargo.toml
+  src/
+    main.rs              # Binary entry point, tracing init, dispatch, exit codes
+    cli.rs               # Top-level Cli struct, Commands enum, global flags
+    client.rs            # SiemClient HTTP wrapper (reqwest + headers)
+    config.rs            # ClientConfig, TOML loading, env var merging
+    error.rs             # CliError enum, exit code mapping
+    output.rs            # OutputFormatter trait, Table/Json/Csv impls
+    commands/
+      mod.rs             # Re-export all command modules
+      query.rs           # QueryArgs + handler
+      rules.rs           # RulesArgs + handler
+      alerts.rs          # AlertsArgs + handler
+      ingest.rs          # IngestArgs + handler
+      config.rs          # ConfigArgs + handler
+      status.rs          # StatusArgs + handler
+      tenant.rs          # TenantArgs + handler
+      login.rs           # LoginArgs + handler
+      completion.rs      # Shell completion generation
+      init.rs            # First-time setup
+```
+
+### Key Dependencies
+
+| Library | Purpose |
+|---------|---------|
+| `clap` 4.x (derive) | Argument parsing, global flags, help generation |
+| `clap_complete` | Shell completion scripts (bash/zsh/fish/PowerShell) |
+| `reqwest` 0.12 (rustls-tls) | HTTP client for API communication |
+| `comfy-table` 7 | Table output with dynamic width, ANSI styling |
+| `keyring` 3 | OS keychain credential storage |
